---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/use-cases/segmentation';
const title = 'Shopify Segmentation that controls who receives a message | ' + site.name;
const desc = 'A segment is useful when it changes an action.';
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
<ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
<section class="container py-16"><a class="link" href="/use-cases">All workflow guides</a><h1 class="hero-title mt-5">Segmentation that controls who receives a message</h1><p class="mt-7 text-xl text-cyan-100">A segment is useful when it changes an action. Define the recipient, the data needed to qualify, the owner and the exit condition before building a larger audience library. Segments describe membership; send-time permission and workflow priority still need their own checks.</p></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Write an audience contract</h2><p>For every active segment record its purpose, required properties, source system, refresh behavior and consuming workflows. Define missing data explicitly: an absent purchase event can mean no purchase, a delayed sync or a disconnected store. Treat these as different states rather than silently classifying all three as prospects.</p><p>Use stable customer and order identifiers. Record timestamp and currency conventions before comparing recency or spend. A customer with multiple email addresses or POS records may be duplicated; matching by a shared phone number alone can also merge different people. Assign identity exceptions to the data owner.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Start with decisions you can act on</h2><p>A non-buyer audience can feed welcome; a purchaser audience should stop that acquisition offer and start appropriate post-purchase education. Category purchasers may need different product guidance. An active subscription must be checked against replenishment and winback. Add a segment only when its message or eligibility differs.</p><p>Consent is a separate dimension. Someone who can receive email may not be eligible for SMS, and a phone number is not an opt-in record. Keep the source and timestamp of each permission. Segment membership must not override unsubscribe handling or turn a transactional notification into a promotional message.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Three proposed data exercises</h2><p>Beauty: distinguish purchased collection from quiz interest and unknown preference. A missing shade answer should get broad product guidance rather than a guessed shade. Wholesale: use approved account status and account owner before including trade pricing; an email domain alone is insufficient. Pet products: distinguish active subscription from a one-time order before a reorder invitation. These are proposed configurations, not merchant case studies.</p><p>For each exercise, create positive, negative and missing-data profiles and inspect why each qualifies. Include a late order update and a refunded order. Keep the result as an acceptance record for the integration owner; audience size alone cannot verify that a boolean condition is correct.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Resolve overlapping journeys explicitly</h2><p>Choose a priority policy for conflicting promotional jobs. A current cart may pause a welcome offer, while a paid order should exit acquisition offers. Essential order notices follow their own rules. Write the policy per message purpose rather than assuming one universal ordering suits every store.</p><p>Recheck the policy at send time after waits. A customer can buy, unsubscribe or enter support escalation while queued. Record both membership and suppression reason so the operator can distinguish a sync defect from an intentional exclusion. Resume only if the original message is still relevant.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Evaluate the platform with real definitions</h2><p>Klaviyo documents dynamic segments and Shopify customer tags. Use those documented inputs as a starting point, then demonstrate the exact order, refund and consent conditions you need. An available property does not prove historical completeness or immediate refresh. Compare a Shopify record with its messaging profile.</p><p>Sequenzy advertises Shopify synchronization and segmentation, and its email billing is based on sends with unlimited contacts. Evaluate whether your required fields and events are usable in the intended branch before migration. Neither send-based billing nor a large segment library proves that audience logic is correct. Keep the simpler existing tool if it can demonstrate the same decisions.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Measure the action and the data</h2><p>Report eligible population, excluded population with reasons, data freshness and unknown-property coverage. If a category preference is missing for most recipients, a highly targeted campaign may simply omit a large part of the business. Show coverage alongside campaign results.</p><p>When testing segmentation strategy, compare alternative treatments among customers who could receive either. Comparing VIP revenue with first-time-buyer revenue does not show that segmentation caused improvement. Record conversion, net contribution after returns, opt-outs and send volume using the same observation window.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Migration and retirement</h2><p>Export definitions, not just audience CSVs. Rebuild conditions against the destination event names, timezone and refund treatment. Compare sample profiles and explain membership differences before enabling new sends. Disable the old executor as part of cutover so duplicate journeys do not survive the migration.</p><p>The retention owner should retire segments that no longer drive an action after checking all campaigns and automations that consume them. Keep a versioned definition and a named replacement rather than deleting a shared tag blindly. Reassess definitions before major catalog or subscription changes.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Supplier scope and current sources</h2><p>Checked 25 November 2026. <a class="link" href="https://apps.shopify.com/sequenzy">Sequenzy’s Shopify listing</a> describes store synchronization and marketing automation. Its <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/pricing">pricing page</a> separates send-based email plans from the paid SMS/MMS beta add-on. Confirm destination support and the complete quote for your intended workload. These supplier descriptions are not independent performance tests.</p><p>The <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/115005251588">Klaviyo glossary</a> documents segments, Shopify tags and separate channel status. Validate the events, permissions and delays for your own configuration; the operational designs above do not claim every supplier implements every step natively.</p></div></section>
<section class="container py-10"><div class="prose-shopify card"><h2>Continue the operating plan</h2><p>Related guides: <a class="link" href="/use-cases/vip-segments">vip segments</a>, <a class="link" href="/use-cases/winback">winback</a>. Compare the required behavior with <a class="link" href="/apps">app reviews</a> and <a class="link" href="/compare">platform comparisons</a>.</p></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
